  "rules": {
    "qualitative_market": "Require an in-scope chemical, accepted identity mapping, eligible compound-level source and an interpretable presence state before qualitative aggregation. Ambiguous CAS records cannot contribute.",
    "historical_market": "Reconstruct the historical best-presence state before the identity/numeric gate for audit comparison only. Do not compute scores or select numeric maxima.",
    "quantity": "Keep raw quantity, bounds, unit, activity, year and jurisdiction. Both annual tonnes and tonnes with unspecified reporting period are retained as candidates; do not annualise, combine or select a maximum. Temporal comparability remains a later selection decision.",
    "gic": "Name-only associations remain review_required. Industrial inventory tags need direct local support on a matched SID and the frozen inventory classification. Unsupported shared-identifier tags are excluded. No-match is a completed lookup, not proof of absence.",
    "gic_metadata": "Classification uses frozen metadata retained by Stage 4C; historical metadata acquisition hashes remain unavailable. No independent current regulatory verification is claimed.",
    "identity_review": "The 15 model-association reviews do not invalidate independent exposure evidence; QSAR/Pov/LRTP isolation remains enforced and no prediction is consumed.",
    "external": "Keep all rows, including out-of-scope rows and failed/no-candidate queries. Nonempty query error messages require review even when a terminal status/count is present; neither partial query coverage nor no CID is a confirmed zero. Audit patent zero-baseline correction and PubMed eligibility without selecting counts or scoring.",
    "provenance": "Canonical production/market tables are frozen derived inputs, not newly reconstructed raw-source transformations. Verify declared primary inputs and raw-file hashes where recorded; record hash gaps explicitly."
  },
